  "lineage": "Post-war European avant-garde composer movement centered on the Internationale Ferienkurse für Neue Musik in Darmstadt (founded 1946), extending Webern's serial-row organization to all musical parameters (pitch, rhythm, dynamics, articulation, register) — \"total serialism\" or \"integral serialism.\" Boulez's Structures Ia (1952), Stockhausen's Kreuzspiel (1951), and Nono's Il canto sospeso (1956) constitute the canonical type-specimens. The Darmstadt School defined the European-modernist mainstream of 1950s-1960s.",
